---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../../config/site';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How JR and Associates, Inc. collects, uses, and protects information connected with the Joe Rossi Umpires Hall of Fame website, donations, and events."
  canonicalPath="/privacy-policy/"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy Policy', path: '/privacy-policy/' }]}
>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <PageHero title="Privacy Policy" intro={`How ${site.legalName} handles information connected with the ${site.name} website.`} />
    <section class="section">
      <article class="page-surface prose policy-copy">
        <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> September 25, 2026</p>

        <h2>At a glance</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>We do not sell, rent, or trade personal information, including donor information.</li>
          <li>Payment card details are entered only on Stripe. They never pass through JRHOF.org or reach the Hall of Fame.</li>
          <li>We use Google Analytics, Google Ads, Microsoft Clarity, and Cloudflare Web Analytics to understand how the site is used and whether our search ads lead to donations. These tools use cookies.</li>
          <li>You can reach us about your information at <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Who publishes this site</h2>
        <p>This website is published by {site.legalName}, a Colorado 501(c)(3) nonprofit organization, for the {site.name}. The organization’s EIN is {site.ein}. This policy covers JRHOF.org and the information we receive through it.</p>

        <h2>Information you give us</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Email.</strong> The site has no contact form. When you email us, we receive your name, email address, and whatever you choose to write or attach, such as a story, a correction, a photograph, or a program.</li>
          <li><strong>Donations.</strong> Online gifts are made on Stripe’s secure checkout page. Stripe shares with us your name, email address, the billing details you give Stripe, and the amount and date of your gift. We never receive your full card number.</li>
          <li><strong>Event purchases.</strong> Items such as mulligans and raffle tickets are also paid for on Stripe. Some events have used Eventbrite for registration; information you give Eventbrite is governed by Eventbrite’s privacy policy, and Eventbrite shares registration details with us so we can run the event.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
        <p>Like most websites, JRHOF.org uses service providers that collect technical information when you visit, such as pages viewed, the site that referred you, device and browser type, approximate location derived from your IP address, and interactions such as clicking a donate, registration, email, or outside link.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the site and protects it from abuse. It processes your IP address and request details to deliver pages. Cloudflare Web Analytics gives us visitor counts without cookies.</li>
          <li><strong>Google Analytics and Google Ads</strong>, loaded through Google Tag Manager, use cookies to measure site use and to tell us when a visit from one of our Google search ads leads to a donation or registration. Google Analytics data is kept for 14 months. Learn <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Microsoft Clarity</strong>, with Microsoft Advertising, captures how visitors use the site through behavioral metrics, heatmaps, and session replay, using first- and third-party cookies. We use it to find pages that are hard to read or use. Clarity is set to mask what visitors type, and Microsoft uses the data as described in the <a href="https://www.microsoft.com/privacy/privacystatement">Microsoft Privacy Statement</a>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How we measure donations</h2>
        <p>To learn which pages and ads lead to gifts without collecting more about you:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>When you select a Stripe donation or payment link, the site adds the random identifier that Google Analytics assigned to your browser. Stripe keeps it with the payment, which lets us compare donations with site visits.</li>
          <li>When Stripe returns you to our thank-you page, the page tells Google Analytics that a donation was completed, using Stripe’s transaction reference so it is counted once. It does not send your name, email address, or the amount of your gift.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Google Maps directions</h2>
        <p>Event pages may provide a link to Google Maps for venue directions and a map created with Google Maps’ standard sharing feature. To avoid an unnecessary Google request when someone only opens the event page, the embedded map loads when the venue section approaches the visitor’s screen. At that point—or if the visitor opens the directions link—the browser connects to Google, which may process the destination, IP address, browser information, and any location information the visitor separately chooses to provide under Google’s own terms and privacy policy. JRHOF does not request the visitor’s device location.</p>

        <h2>How we use information</h2>
        <p>We use information to answer your questions, review corrections and historical materials, process and acknowledge donations, provide receipts and any tax acknowledgments the law requires, run events, keep accurate financial and organizational records, protect the site, and improve the website and our outreach.</p>

        <h2>Donor privacy</h2>
        <p>We use donor information only to process, acknowledge, and account for gifts and to keep the organization’s records. We do not sell, rent, trade, or share donor names or contact information with other organizations for their own use, and we do not publish a donor’s name or gift amount without the donor’s permission.</p>

        <h2>Photographs and the Hall of Fame archive</h2>
        <p>Hall of Fame events are photographed, and selected photographs are published in the event archive on JRHOF.org. Inductee biographies are public records of service to Colorado baseball. If you would like a photograph of yourself reviewed for removal, or a biography corrected, email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a> with the page address. We review every request.</p>

        <h2>Information sharing</h2>
        <p>We share information only with service providers that help us operate: Cloudflare (hosting and security), Stripe (payments), Eventbrite (registration for events that use it), Google (analytics, advertising measurement, and maps), Microsoft (Clarity analytics), and the provider that hosts the organization’s email. Each processes information under its own terms and privacy policy.</p>
        <p>We may also disclose information when the law requires it, or when needed to protect the organization, its supporters, or the public. The organization does not sell personal information.</p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings. The site works without them.</li>
          <li>Google offers a <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a> and <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/">My Ad Center</a> for managing ad personalization.</li>
          <li>You can ask us what information we hold about you, or ask us to correct or delete it, by emailing <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>. We may need to keep some donation and financial records to meet accounting and tax requirements.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Retention</h2>
        <p>We keep email correspondence as long as it is useful to answer you or to preserve Hall of Fame records. We keep donation and financial records as long as accounting and tax law require. Materials you share for the archive may be kept permanently as part of the historical record.</p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>Payments are handled by Stripe, a PCI-compliant payment processor. The site is served only over HTTPS and uses modern security headers. We limit access to donor and event information to the volunteers who need it. No website or internet transmission can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>This site is intended for a general audience and does not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If a parent or guardian believes a child has sent us personal information, please email us and we will delete it.</p>

        <h2>External links</h2>
        <p>The site links to other websites, including CHSBUA, Stripe, Google Maps, and event resources. We are not responsible for the privacy practices of external sites.</p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>We will update this page when our practices change, and the date at the top shows the latest version.</p>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>For privacy questions or requests, email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a> or use the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>. Please do not send payment card numbers or other sensitive financial information by email.</p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy-copy { margin-inline: auto; }
</style>
